---
// EN legal content · Privacy Policy · copied verbatim from src/pages/en/legal/privacy.astro
// Language switcher uses absolute zymplo.com URLs so it works the same embedded
// under any country subdomain.
// 🔴 FIXED 2026-08-18 (FUEGO 5): this comment used to claim same-language internal
// links could stay bare (/legal/...) because "the country is already encoded in the
// subdomain" — that was never measured and was FALSE. Measured 2026-08-18 15:52 -03:
// br.zymplo.com/legal/privacy/ returns <html lang="es">, not pt-BR. All those links
// now go through `base` (see below).
// 2026-11-02 · text corrected so it says what the code does (controller by country, AI and voice providers, retention, transfer basis). The same text lives in src/pages/en/legal/privacy.astro: edit them together.
export const meta = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy · Zymplo',
  description: 'How Zymplo collects, uses and protects your personal data. LGPD · GDPR · CCPA compliance.',
  lastUpdated: '2026-11-02',
};
// OPS fix(links): `base` es el prefijo (país o idioma) del contexto donde
// se renderiza este documento — '' en el apex ES, '/en' o '/pt' en el apex
// de idioma, '/{slug}' bajo /[country]/legal/*. Todo link interno "mismo
// contexto, otro documento" tiene que pasar por acá — un valor fijo tipo
// '/legal/...' ignora el contexto y manda siempre al documento en español
// del apex (medido 2026-08-18: br.zymplo.com/legal/privacy/ → lang=es).
export interface Props { base: string }
const { base } = Astro.props;

---
<header>
  <a href="https://zymplo.com/"><img src="/brand/isotipo.svg" alt="Zymplo" /></a>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: {meta.lastUpdated} · Effective since: 2026-05-04</p>
  <p class="meta"><a href="https://zymplo.com/legal/privacy/">Español</a> · <a href="https://zymplo.com/pt/legal/privacy/">Português</a> · English</p>
</header>

<div class="box">
  <strong>Quick summary:</strong> Zymplo receives your WhatsApp messages to process them with AI and return useful responses (reminders · payment collection · invoices · etc). We do not sell your data · we do not share it with advertising third parties · you can delete your account whenever you want at <a href={`${base}/legal/delete-account/`}>/legal/delete-account/</a>.
</div>

<h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
<p>The company responsible for processing your personal data (the "controller" under Brazil's LGPD) depends on the country:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Brazil:</strong> <strong>Zymplo Brasil LTDA</strong> · CNPJ 66.667.634/0001-00 · Fortaleza, CE.</li>
  <li><strong>Paraguay:</strong> <strong>Zymplo S.A.</strong> · RUC 80170149-0 · San Lorenzo.</li>
  <li><strong>All other countries:</strong> <strong>Zymplo Inc.</strong> · Delaware (USA) · EIN 30-1486305 · DUNS 145007664 · Newark, DE 19713, USA.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Data protection officer (DPO):</strong> José Carlos Rolón. Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:privacy@zymplo.com">privacy@zymplo.com</a>.</p>

<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp messages</strong> you send to the Zymplo number (text · audio · images · documents · location).</li>
  <li><strong>Your phone number</strong> (provided automatically by Meta's API when you write).</li>
  <li><strong>Conversation metadata:</strong> timestamps · detected language · country detected via phone prefix.</li>
  <li><strong>Data you share voluntarily:</strong> client names · collection amounts · photos of receipts · document numbers (CPF · RUC · RFC · etc · only the ones you choose to use).</li>
  <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> which tools you used (collection · NFS-e · reminders · etc) · no advertising tracking.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What we do NOT collect</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Your WhatsApp contact list.</li>
  <li>Messages from other chats that are NOT with Zymplo.</li>
  <li>Your GPS location (unless you explicitly share it).</li>
  <li>Biometric data · sensitive information unrelated to your business.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. What we use your data for</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Process your messages with AI models and transcribe your voice messages (providers in section 5).</li>
  <li>Execute the actions you requested (create a payment collection · send a reminder · issue an NFS-e · etc).</li>
  <li>Improve service quality (aggregated and anonymized analytics).</li>
  <li>Comply with local legal obligations (LGPD Brazil · Law 1682/01 Paraguay · etc).</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Legal bases</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Consent:</strong> where consent is the applicable basis, it is always explicit, informed and specific, and may be withdrawn at any time. For other purposes we process your data on the basis of performance of a contract, compliance with a legal obligation, or legitimate interest, in accordance with Art. 7 of the LGPD. We do not rely on implicit consent.</li>
  <li><strong>Contract performance:</strong> to deliver the service you requested.</li>
  <li><strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> for fraud prevention and service improvement.</li>
  <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> retention of issued NFS-e for the fiscal period (5 years in Brazil).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Who we share with</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Meta (WhatsApp Business API):</strong> messaging infrastructure.</li>
  <li><strong>AI and voice providers</strong> (they process the content of your messages in real time; all are headquartered in the US, except DeepSeek):
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Text and images:</strong> Anthropic (Claude).</li>
      <li><strong>Voice-message transcription:</strong> Groq (primary), Deepgram and OpenAI (backup).</li>
      <li><strong>Short support tasks</strong> (for example, understanding your name or classifying a request): OpenAI and xAI; and, only if enabled in the service, Groq, Cerebras, Together AI and DeepSeek (China).</li>
      <li><strong>Conversation quality log:</strong> LangSmith (LangChain), only when that log is switched on in the server.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Stripe / Mercado Pago:</strong> only if you activate payment features.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloudflare · Oracle Cloud:</strong> hosting · CDN.</li>
  <li><strong>Resend:</strong> transactional emails.</li>
  <li><strong>Authorities:</strong> only under a valid court order from the corresponding country.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do NOT sell · do NOT rent · do NOT share for advertising.</p>
<p>We do not use your data to train AI models unless you accept this on an optional, separate basis.</p>

<h2>6. Google data (Google Calendar)</h2>
<p>If you connect your Google account, Zymplo requests the minimum events permission for your <strong>Google Calendar</strong> (<code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events</code>) so that, from WhatsApp, you can:</p>
<ul>
  <li>See the events on your agenda for the day.</li>
  <li>Create, update and delete events and appointments at your request (including payment collections and reminders).</li>
</ul>
<p>We process that data in real time to execute what you requested · we do not keep copies of your calendar on our servers beyond what is necessary for the active feature. You can disconnect your account and revoke access at any time from <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">your Google account</a> or by asking via WhatsApp.</p>
<div class="box">
  <strong>Limited Use (Google API Services User Data Policy):</strong> Zymplo's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its <em>Limited Use</em> requirements. Specifically: we do not use your Google Calendar data for advertising · we do not sell it or transfer it to third parties, except to operate the feature you requested, under a valid legal requirement, or with your explicit consent · and we do not use it to train generalized AI models.
</div>

<h2>7. Retention</h2>
<p>The periods below count from your account's last activity. You can ask for deletion earlier, whenever you want (section 8).</p>
<ul>
  <li>Personal identification data (name · email · phone · CPF/CNPJ): anonymized after 90 days (free plan) or 7 years (paid plan).</li>
  <li>Conversations with the assistant: 30 days (free plan) or 12 months (paid plan), unless you have optionally accepted their use for training.</li>
  <li>Issued NFS-e: 5 years (free plan) or 7 years (paid plan), by fiscal obligation.</li>
  <li>Technical logs: 90 days.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Your rights (LGPD · GDPR · CCPA)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Access:</strong> request a copy of all your data.</li>
  <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> correct inaccurate data.</li>
  <li><strong>Deletion ("right to be forgotten"):</strong> see <a href={`${base}/legal/delete-account/`}>/legal/delete-account/</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Portability:</strong> export your data in JSON.</li>
  <li><strong>Objection:</strong> refuse non-essential uses.</li>
  <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent:</strong> at any time without affecting prior processing.</li>
  <li><strong>Information about consent:</strong> to know that you may refuse consent and what the consequences are.</li>
  <li><strong>Complaint to the authority:</strong> in Brazil, to the ANPD (National Data Protection Authority) against the controller; in other countries, to your local authority (section 13).</li>
</ul>
<p>Exercise your rights by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@zymplo.com">privacy@zymplo.com</a>. We respond within 15 days at most.</p>

<h2>9. Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256).</li>
  <li>Role-restricted data access · audit logs.</li>
  <li>Encrypted backups · disaster recovery tested monthly.</li>
  <li>Quarterly key rotation policy.</li>
</ul>
<p>If a security incident affects your personal data, we will notify you and the competent authority. In Brazil, the deadline is 3 business days from the moment we learn that the incident affected personal data (ANPD Res. CD/ANPD No. 15/2024).</p>

<h2>10. Minors</h2>
<p>Zymplo is NOT directed at anyone under 18. If we discover a minor's data, we delete it immediately. If you are a guardian and notice this: <a href="mailto:privacy@zymplo.com">privacy@zymplo.com</a>.</p>

<h2>11. International transfers</h2>
<p>Some of the providers in section 5 are outside your country, mainly in the United States, so your data may be processed in the USA · Brazil · Paraguay · countries where our providers operate.</p>
<p>Basis for these transfers: your specific and prominent consent (LGPD, art. 33, VIII). We are arranging with the providers the adoption of the ANPD's standard contractual clauses (the "cláusulas-padrão", approved by Brazil's data protection authority); this process is under way.</p>

<h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We will notify you via WhatsApp of any material changes · 30 days in advance. Minor changes (typographical · clarifications) without notification.</p>

<h2>13. Regulatory authority</h2>
<p>You can file a complaint with your local authority: ANPD (Brazil) · MITIC (Paraguay) · INAI (Mexico) · AEPD (Spain) · SIC (Colombia) · etc.</p>

<footer>
  <p>Brazil: Zymplo Brasil LTDA · CNPJ 66.667.634/0001-00 · Fortaleza CE · Paraguay: Zymplo S.A. · RUC 80170149-0 · San Lorenzo · All other countries: Zymplo Inc. · Delaware USA · EIN 30-1486305 · DUNS 145007664</p>
  <p><a href="/">Back to zymplo.com</a> · <a href={`${base}/legal/terms/`}>Terms of Service</a> · <a href={`${base}/legal/delete-account/`}>Delete account</a></p>
</footer>
